; S1a.3.1 — an unbound relation head in a `:match` premise.
;
; `?R` is not a parameter, so the activator cannot bind it, and M1 matches
; relations per activator (Q29). Until S1.22.0 the relation compiler returned
; no steps here — dropping the premise. The plan's only premise gone, `steps`
; is empty, and the matcher reads an empty step list as one VACUOUS match, so
; the rule fired unconditionally and stored its conclusion.
;
; Compile-negative until M1e2 S1e2.2.24 (W24, the stage's default 1): the
; compiler refused the head with a CompileError in the Python IR's spelling,
; `unbound relation head ?R in a premise of SForm(…)`. Since then the loader
; refuses a relation variable no parameter binds, at the top level as inside a
; pattern, and this file moved here from `examples/broken/compile/`.
(relation p Thing)

(rule uses-free-head (?S)
  :match  (?R ?x)
  :assert (p ?x))

(uses-free-head p)
